@Notes for programmers: Use "Getlistingstatus" to check the list according to the ID
@Note by scripts: use `Setlistingstatus` to change the status of the list in this script
Use: This script displays information about the list during double -click. It also has a function that updates the list of the list by editing this property in GUI or changing the value of the variable in the text block.
Right -click any entry in the list. Select "List details" in the menu displayed. The menu will expand and include a list of list details. Then you can expand these elements in the same way as you want to see detailed information. When you start clicking something twice to get more information, you will need a "divided window". Do it in the upper left corner, right above the icon of the program. In this way, you can display all open things on one screen without having to return to different windows, which is tedious.
